              a: 'Thermal throttling is when a processor automatically reduces its clock speed to prevent overheating. For local LLMs, speed can drop during long inference sessions; illustratively, a MacBook Pro M4 Max might fall from about 35 tok/sec to roughly 18–22 tok/sec after about 18 minutes (estimate, not measured by PromptQuorum; it varies by chassis, ambient temperature and software). Desktops have larger cooling systems and are far less likely to throttle in normal use.',
